sentences.l:
And he held a wand in his hands,
fine, golden, with which the eyes of men he charms,
of whomever he wishes, and others again, even sleeping, he wakes;

And as when bats in the innermost-recess of a wondrous cave
squeaking flutter, whenever one has fallen off
from the chain, from the rock, and to one another they cling,
so they, squeaking, went along together;

And past the streams of Oceanus they went, and the White Rock,
and past the gates of the Sun and the land of dreams
they went;

and close by
came next the soul of Agamemnon, Atreus’ son,
grieving;

and around you others
were being killed, of Trojans and of Achaeans the sons, the best,
fighting over you;

But when we had carried you to the ships out of the war,
we laid you on a bier, having cleansed your fine skin
with warm water and with oil;

and now they would have gone, springing up, to the hollow ships,
if a man had not held them back, knowing things old and many,
Nestor, whose counsel earlier too appeared best;

and many Achaean heroes
moved vigorously in arms around the pyre of (you) burning,
both on foot and horsemen;

But when the flame of Hephaestus had finished you off,
at dawn then we gathered your white bones, Achilles,
in unmixed wine and oil;

Already at the burial of many men you have been present,
of heroes, whenever once a king has died
the young men gird themselves and make ready the contests;

but those you would most of all have wondered at in your heart on seeing,
such as upon you set down the goddess, very fair contest-prizes,
silver-footed Thetis;
